1855","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2480121},"ottId":706781,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Touit","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Touit is a genus of Neotropical parrots in the family Psittacidae. The genus was introduced by the English zoologist George Robert Gray in 1855 with the scarlet-shouldered parrotlet (Touit huetii) as the type species.","revisionId":1319563960,"title":"Touit","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touit","wikidataId":"Q1192076"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Canada Goose","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Greater Canada Goose","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Canada Goose (canadensis Group)","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"},{"language":"en","name":"Canada Goose, Greater Canada Goose","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Branta canadensis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Branta canadensis (Linnaeus, 1758)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":5232437},"ottId":714461,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Branta canadensis","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Canada goose (Branta canadensis) is a large species of goose with a black head and neck, white cheeks, white under its chin, and a brown body. It is native to the Arctic and temperate regions of North America, and it is occasionally found during migration across the Atlantic in northern Europe.","revisionId":1375166117,"title":"Canada goose","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada_goose","wikidataId":"Q26733"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Pig","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Boar","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Wild Pig","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Feral Hog","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Feral Pig","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Wild Boar","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Sus scrofa","confidence":99